.page cal 1 show a calendar

# SYNOPSIS
*cal* [[_MONTH_] _YEAR_]

# DESCRIPTION
`cal` prints a calendar. Without arguments it shows the current month, with today's date in reverse video when output goes to a terminal. With one argument (a year) it prints all twelve months of that year; with two, the given month (1 to 12) of the given year. Weeks start on Sunday. Dates are those of the proleptic Gregorian calendar, in UTC.

# EXAMPLES
    cal
    cal 2 2024
    cal 1999

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 for a month outside 1 to 12.

# SEE ALSO
date(1), uptime(1)
